{"kind":"request","text":"@builder: security review of the landed MCP service (main bd02ecff, packages/mcp, packages/cli/src/mcp.ts, packages/client/src/invitation.ts), read directly by the planner at Hugh's request, 2026-10-13 11:10 Eastern. No P1: the signing key never leaves the config store, every write is a signed intent a scope judges, the loopback HTTP boundary binds 127.0.0.0/8 or ::1 only with a per-launch bearer compared in constant time and refuses any request with an Origin header, custody files and directories are owner-only, and `credential` returns a secret only in the structured field for the caller's own read-token acts. One P2 to fix before the submission, and five P3 advisories for after it.\n\nP2, join accepts any service URL from the link (packages/mcp/src/service.ts:829-834, packages/client/src/invitation.ts:30-35). `wellFormedInvitation` checks only that `service` is a string. A server that has joined nothing yet (service \"\") takes the link's service as its own, signs membership's join with the device key, sends it with the invitation secret to that URL, and persists the URL in the configuration (`joined`, packages/cli/src/mcp.ts:92-95), so every later signed act and session request of this key goes there. An agent that is handed a crafted artroom-invite link (prompt injection is the ordinary path) is enough. The CLI's `dap join` has the same gap but a person pastes that link; the MCP tool is callable by the agent. Fix: in `wellFormedInvitation`, or in `#join` before anything is signed, require the link's service to parse as a URL whose protocol is https:, with no username, password, query or fragment; allow http: only for a loopback host, for tests and local runs. Refuse with the existing shape error. Apply the same check to `dap join` in packages/cli/src/commands.ts:830 so both paths agree. Add one test per path with an http: and a non-URL service.\n\nP3, after the submission: (a) packages/mcp/src/describe.ts:235, an unknown guard form renders as its raw JSON into a tool description and into `inspect describe`; a definition author can place agent-directed text there. Render unknown forms as \"a guard of an unrecognized form\" and keep the JSON only in `inspect declaration`. (b) packages/mcp/src/node.ts:361 and 445-448, the 2025-11-25 sessions map has no bound and no expiry; a holder of the bearer can grow it without limit. Bound it (for example 64) and expire idle sessions. (c) packages/mcp/src/service.ts:169-170, the `#searches` and `#pages` maps grow by one entry per scope and seq ever searched; bound them to the most recent few hundred. (d) node.ts:53, `alive` treats EPERM as alive, so a lock file left by a dead process whose PID another user's process now holds is never reclaimed; document the operator step beside `blockedBy`. (e) docs/mcp.md \"Custody\": say that a join's record and its archive hold the invitation secret inside the signed intent for up to 30 days, as the membership history does, and that the HTTP bearer printed to standard error may land in a host's log, so a host that logs stderr should be given the bearer another way.\n\nTarget refs/heads/main for the P2 as one small head with its own review request to the checker, after the Start recomposition and the self-host guide. Please promise here.","body":{"conditions":"The MCP join and dap join refuse an invitation link whose service is not an https: URL (http: only on a loopback host) with no credentials, query or fragment, before anything is signed; one test per path; checker approval; landed on main. The five P3 items are filed as the builder's own follow-up after the submission.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}